# Entrypoint for the cloud trees lane: the sixteen city models and NOTHING
# else — no cross-city `data_source` merge, no full_tree_info rollup. That
# absence is the entire point of this file, so do not "complete" it by
# importing tree_info or copying its merge block.
#
# A city's parquet build proves completeness by unioning its partitions
# (municipal + community + OSM) over the city's per-city source enum. That
# proof only resolves in an environment where the city's keys are unmerged
# and the cross-city rollup datasource is out of scope. Planned through
# tree_info.preql instead, the planner satisfies a city's rows from
# full_tree_info_v2.parquet — the rollup built FROM the city parquets — and
# the build goes circular: Athens's first cloud build this way produced a
# parquet holding only the OSM staging partition (13,248 rows, zero
# municipal), with its watermark advanced so nothing ever looked stale.
# Verified both ways by dry-run: through this file Athens plans as the
# three-partition UNION ALL; through tree_info.preql it plans as a read of
# the rollup (or, declared partial, of the staging parquet alone).
#
# The old single cloud job never hit this because its entrypoint was the
# `raw` directory, and directory execution plans each preql file in its own
# environment. The platform's [[cloud.job]] entries require a file
# entrypoint, so this file recreates that isolation explicitly.
#
# full_tree_info still rebuilds every tick: tree_enrichment.preql imports
# tree_info, so the enrichment lane (offset an hour after this one) picks up
# the stale rollup and builds it from the city parquets this lane just
# refreshed. The residual hazard — a city going stale between the two lanes
# gets circularly recycled by the enrichment lane's environment — is
# documented on that job in ../trilogy.toml.

import ussfo.sf_tree_info;
import usnyc.nyc_tree_info;
import usbos.boston_tree_info;
import frpar.paris_tree_info;
import usbtv.burlington_tree_info;
import cavan.vancouver_tree_info;
import deber.berlin_tree_info;
import nlams.amsterdam_tree_info;
import gblon.london_tree_info;
import aumel.melbourne_tree_info;
import arbue.buenosaires_tree_info;
import uslax.losangeles_tree_info;
import uswas.washingtondc_tree_info;
import ustem.tempe_tree_info;
import grath.athens_tree_info;
import grmlo.milos_tree_info;
